    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0602" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/2585</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.32 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1789. My 1785, March 13, regarding <hi rendition="#italic">Taurus</hi>.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d495-f1"/> Foreign Office informs me, it has been decided to
                    place in prize court in addition to items mentioned in above cable consignments
                    meat and lard shipped by Armour to Armour of Goteborg and by Swift and Company
                    to Peder Mellin of Göteborg.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
